-- title:
--   Order zero of one-sided Gauss residues at fixed non-node places
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M>0$ with $p\mid M$ but $p^{2}\nmid M$, a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ containing every unit that reduces to $1$ in $\mathbb Z/(M/p)$, with $M/p$ nonzero, and assume `jqModC ℚ` lies in the level-one $q$-expansion field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`; let $\mathfrak X$ be a structure `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a valuation subring in which $p$ is a non-unit, with residue field $\kappa$ algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho\colon R\,p\to A$ compatible with the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Write $\bar F$ for the $q$-expansion function field of `ΓN p M H hpM` over $\kappa$, $F_M=$`xHFunctionFieldBar M H` and $F_{M/p}=$`xHFunctionFieldBar (M/p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)`. Let $\delta$ be the action on places of $\bar F$ of the semilinear automorphism attached by `diamondActionModL` to a $\Gamma_0(M/p)$-lift of a unit $pb$ of $\mathbb Z/(M/p)$ whose underlying element is $p$; let $SS$ be the finite set of pairs $s$ with $s.2$ a supersingular place and $s.1=$`qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL` of $s.2$. Let $\theta$ be an $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism of $F_M$ commuting with the arithmetic Galois action, $\alpha\colon F_{M/p}\to F_M$ an integral $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra map which is the identity on $q$-expansions, with $\theta\circ\alpha$ integral and acting on $q$-expansions by `qExpand (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) p`; let $Psp$ be a `JHPlaceSpecialization` for these data and $Rpd$ a `ProlongationDatum` for $Psp$ and $\theta$, consisting of two regular prolongations $R_1,R_2$ of $A$ to $F_M$ with values in $\bar F$. Assume the type dichotomy, the model law, the order law at fixed affine places, the regularity and node-value laws for $SS$, cusp coverage (each place of $\bar F$ at which no element with $q$-expansion `jqModC κ` takes a value in $\kappa$ is both the first reading of an $\infty$-side cusp and the second reading of a $0$-side cusp), the transport law `hwgen` for points of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{Meta}$ under $\theta$, and the two compatibilities `hcompat`, `hcompat'` of the places of the fibre model with the two readings and with the Frobenius of places (these hypotheses are summarised here). Then two symmetric assertions hold. First, for every $g\in F_M$ in the integers of $R_1$ with $R_1$-residue nonzero, and every place $v$ of $\bar F$ over $\kappa$ which is fixed in the sense that `qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL` of $\delta($`qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL` $v)$ equals $v$, which is not the first coordinate of any $s\in SS$, and such that every place $V$ of $F_M$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $Psp.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,\alpha\,V=v$ satisfies $V.\mathrm{ord}\,g=0$, one has $v.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $R_1$-residue of $g$ equal to $0$. Second, the same statement with $R_1$ replaced by $R_2$, $\mathrm{reduceFst}\,\alpha$ by $\mathrm{reduceSnd}\,(\theta\circ\alpha)\,\delta$, and first coordinates of elements of $SS$ by second coordinates.
--
--   This is the reading of a one-sided Gauss-valuation residue at a fixed place of the special fibre away from the supersingular crossings: no zero or pole of $g$ above such a place forces the residue to have order zero there. It is one of the local laws used in assembling the place-specialisation and prolongation data for the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ at a prime exactly dividing the level, which in turn supports the comparison of the two components of the special fibre in the level-lowering argument.
